  heading: "Bundi",

  html: "<p>Bundi is the undiscovered splendour, 36 kms from Kota ruled by the Hada Chauhans. First destination is HADOTI. Set in a narrow inclining gorge. The palaces and forts have fairy tale quality about them. Isolated and independent, this picturesque location has much to offer. Rajput architecture shines and in the intricately carved brackets, pillars etc. Interesting places are Diwan-e- aam, Hati Pol, and Naubat Khana. The small sleepy town of Bundi, a rather unexplored city with rich historical wealth, is surrounded by the Aravali hills on three sides and is circumscribed by a massive wall with four gateways. Impressive medieval forts, palaces and temples with beautiful stone idols and chhatris (Cenotaphs) with carved pillars along with a scenic lake in the heart of the town that add to its charm</p>\n<p>Bundi is one of the erstwhile princely states of Rajasthan, India. A must-visit tourist destination during your Rajasthan travel, Bundi, a small rustic town, is known for its palaces, baolis (step wells) and water tanks. The monuments and their architecture reflect the splendor of the local Rajput chiefs. The walls of the palaces at Bundi are decorated with life-size frescoes depicting the glory of its rulers.</p>\n<p>Bundi came under the Chauhan rulers in the 12th century and was an important state at the peak of Rajput glory in medieval times. The association with the Mughals led to the decline of Bundi. Although the state lost its glory, it continued to be an independent state within the British rule and became a part of India when it gained independence in 1947. Tourism in Bundi opens a world of monumental marvels, especially the Taragarh Fort. The Taragarh Fort, built in 1354, with its imposing structure of stone, is situated on a steep hill and has massive battlements and ramparts. The fort welcomes vacationers through an enormous gateway. Once inside the fort, visitors can see the Bhim Burj, the largest battlement, and a huge water reservoir carved out of solid rock. From the fort, one can see the entire town.</p>\n<p>The Taragarh Fort also is a magnificent point to see the sunset over the Rajasthan horizon. Bundi Palace, which is situated on a hill, adjacent to the Taragarh Fort, is known for its traditional murals. These murals give the traveler a glimpse of the splendor and lifestyle of the rulers of Bundi and their exploits. Though most parts of the palace walls are decorated with traditional murals, only the Chitra Shala area is open for tourists.</p>\n<p>Bundi is also famous for its waterworks (baolis). It has a number of impressive baolis or step wells. Raniji-ki-Baoli, (Queen's step well) is an important place to visit. It is a 46-m-deep step well, built in 1699 by Queen Nathavatji, and is known for its carvings. The Nagar Sagar Kund, a pair of identical, step wells is near Raniji-ki-Baoli, in the center of the town. Nawal Sagar, the artificial lake near the palace is a good tourist spot and one can see a shrine at the center of this lake. Other waterworks worth exploring are the Dhabhai Kund and the Bhora-ji-ka-Kund.</p>\n<h4>Places of Interest: </h4>\n<p>Taragarh Fort or Star Fort, Palace, Chitra Mahal, Phool Sagar Palace, Nagar Sagar Kund, Sukh Mahal, Shikar Burj, Rani Ki Baori.</p>\n<h4>Reach: </h4>\n<p><strong>By Air: </strong>Nearest airport is Jaipur: 206 kms. </p>\n<p><strong>By Rail:</strong> Nearest railhead is Kota: 36 kms. </p>\n<p><strong>By Road:</strong> Jaipur: 206 kms, Kota: 36 kms, Chittaurgarh: 121 kms and Jaipur: 206 kms.</p>\n<h4>How to plan your tours:</h4>\n<p>Rajasthan travel agents and tour operators offers information of Bundi, Bundi tourist places, hotels in Bundi, Bundi sightseeing tours, places of interest in Bundi, Shopping in Bundi, climate and temperature , people, culture, distances from Bundi to other tourist destinations of Rajasthan, Bundi Kota tours, Bundi forts and palaces, Bundi monuments trip, we also offers off beat tours of Kumbhalgarh, Luni, Mukundgarh, Nawalgarh, Rohetgarh, Nathdwara, Karauli, Jhalawar, Eklingji, Ghanerao, Kumbhalgarh, rural royal heritage palace tours, unique and off beat wacky, interesting places tours of Rajasthan, we offers tours with car rental, hotel booking, detailed tour planning, day to day tour itineraries, car with experienced driver, air conditioned car and coaches, hotel bookings and reservation of budget, luxury, deluxe and heritage hotels. Travel and tips to overseas tourists vacations tours, we provide private tours with personal car and driver with your family, individuals, singles, couples, honeymooners, single female travelers. To see the incomparable well designed tour programme of most exotic tourist destinations of all over India: please visit: http://www.india- tourism.net/itineraries.htm aand for any travel query please mails us at: <a href=\"mailto:sales@india-tourism.net\">sales@india-tourism.net</a> To plan out the tour programme and cost, please inform us: nos. of days for the tour, nos. of person traveling together, preferred destinations, travel period, category of the hotels any specific requirement.To justify our credibility, please visit at: www.india-tourism.net/testimonial.htm</p>\n<div"
